[E-TYPE-MISMATCH] Error: `+` gives a `Nat` or an `Int`
    ╭─[ reject/ability-row-arguments.sw:15:43 ]
    │
 15 │ def bad: Nat := both (o => Nat) parser() (1 + 1)
    │                                           ──┬──  
    │                                             ╰──── but `{Parse Char} Nat` is expected here
    │ 
    │ Note 1: on other types `+` is `Add.add`, and there's no `Add` instance for `{Parse Char} Nat` here
    │ 
    │ Note 2: its operations are the row `{Parse Char}`'s, but what they give back is `o => Nat`, not the row's `Std.Effect.PlusRes ((result of Parse) Char) Std.Effect.NoRes`: so it isn't a computation in `{Parse Char}`, and a value here isn't made into one
    │ 
    │ Note 3: for a computation in a row, write the row and let the `Comp` be made from it: `{e} a` for any row, `{} a` for the empty one
────╯
